        "object": "<p>LA added Myles Garrett and brought Aaron Donald out of retirement to create the NFL’s most menacing defense. A Super Bowl trip still isn’t a guarantee</p><p>Last Saturday night, NFL Network premiered the 2025 edition of America’s Game, the annual NFL Films-produced documentary on the reigning Super Bowl champions, this time starring the Seattle Seahawks.</p><p>Less than 24 hours later, the Los Angeles Rams announced that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/aug/30/all-time-great-aaron-donald-comes-out-of-retirement-to-rejoin-stacked-la-rams\">they had lured Aaron Donald</a> out of retirement and signed him to a one-year, $20m contract that could reach $30m with incentives.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/02/los-angeles-rams-aaron-donald-myles-garrett-matthew-stafford\">Continue reading...</a>"
